Yep. 2.6 confirmed the problem wasn't the voice toggle logic anymore — it was the UI location of Read Aloud.
Current ChatGPT web UI has been moving Read Aloud into the More actions / overflow menu, and independent current implementations are using the voice-play-turn-action-button test ID plus the More actions menu path.
OpenAI Developer Community
+1
So I built QSV 2.7 as a fresh complete source from the 2.6 baseline. It now:
checks for the direct Read Aloud control first;
if absent, finds the newest response's More actions control;
opens that menu using a real browser click;
looks for Read aloud inside the menu;
closes the menu after capability probing;
keeps the simple voice OFF/ON capability model;
leaves the relay machinery alone.
Python compilation passed.
